        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "short": "Zoom in",
      "title": "Low-level design: inside one box",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "body": "Now open the Orders box. LLD decides **how one component is built**: the modules or classes it is made of, the interfaces between them, its tables and indexes, its algorithms and its error handling.\n\nHere a controller takes HTTP requests, an order service holds the rules, a repository talks to the database, and a client wraps the calls to Payments.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Keeping the database and other services behind small interfaces (the yellow parts) is what makes the core logic easy to test — see *Testing*."
      },
      "changes": [
        "- The rest of the system",
        "+ Inside Orders: controller, service, repository, payment client"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "zoom": "one service",
        "unit": "classes · tables · states",
        "output": "class & schema design"
      },
