    {
      "id": "s6",
      "short": "Contracts",
      "title": "Where they meet: contracts",
      "chapter": "insight",
      "body": "The two levels meet at the edges of each box. HLD fixes what a component **promises** — its API and the events it publishes. LLD decides **how** it keeps that promise.\n\nThat split is what lets teams work independently: Orders can rewrite everything inside its box, as long as `POST /orders` and `OrderPlaced` keep meaning the same thing.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Changing a contract is an HLD change: other teams must agree, and old and new versions must work side by side for a while (see *REST, RPC & GraphQL* on versioning)."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ The contract at the edge of the service"
      ],
      "metrics": {
