    {
      "id": "s7",
      "short": "Top-down",
      "title": "Case: designing at the wrong level",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "body": "Asked to design this app in an interview, one candidate spends twenty minutes on class diagrams and never mentions that courier locations arrive 40,000 times a second. Another draws perfect boxes, but can’t say how an order avoids being charged twice.\n\nWork **top-down**: requirements, rough numbers, the HLD — then dive into the one or two places where the hard problems are, and do *those* at the LLD level.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "A design session usually runs: requirements → estimates → API → data model → HLD → deep dives → failure cases. The walkthroughs that follow use exactly this order."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Back to the whole system",
        "+ Deep dives: location writes, double charges"
      ],
